  "applicability_scope": [
    "User-reported Level 1 review of all P13 Overview theorem statements except theorem_9_representative_endgame, plus every definition required to interpret the five included statements.",
    "Theorem 1: For each requested finite prefix, one globally valid generator realizes a positive time vector matching the canonical Procedure-1 vector on that prefix and Pareto-optimal there.",
    "Theorem 4: Every monotone unbounded scheduler gives the displayed positive time vector: the maximum of scheduler-entry time and canonical complexity plus one.",
    "Theorem 5: Finite canonical-complexity sublevels suffice for a generator realizing the entire canonical positive Pareto-optimal vector.",
    "Theorem 6: The concrete noisy scheduler based on corrected Procedure 2 realizes the displayed positive noisy time vector, with empty witnesses and zero complexity when no candidate exists.",
    "Theorem 8: Finite noisy-complexity sublevels make the corrected canonical noisy vector realizable and Pareto-optimal.",
    "Standard and noisy realizability, finite-history generators, injective histories, distinct sample cardinality, input-relative freshness, positive time vectors, Pareto comparison, prefix matching/optimality, and finite complexity sublevels.",
    "Canonical Procedure-1 and corrected Procedure-2 definitions, candidate/score/witness semantics, insertion order, greedy scans, fresh selection, schedulers, entry times, canonical complexities, concrete named generators, and recursive project-local defining dependencies.",
    "Arbitrary indexed sets on an infinite ambient type; source instances retain the paper's infinite-language convention. The source noisy pairs are represented by flattened language/noise coordinates, with distinct exceptions at the injective-history boundary.",
    "Existing semantic qualifications, the missing repeated-history adapter, corrected Procedure-2 empty-witness/zero-score convention, source assessments, and arXiv-v1 scope are retained."
  ],
